    # NIGHTFALL SHELF CHRONICLE
    ## Entry ☽-VII-4.91 — Terrace Momiou Conflagration and Aftermath
    
    Filed during the third rotation of the Shadow Parliament following events at Terrace Momiou. Period: Faction Wars, mid-era. Recorded by Factor Umbrae ☽'Viaisnaum, Senior Archivist, ☽'ofund' Guild Registry, Nightfall Shelf. Authenticated under Lex∴andatum, Pactum∴silenti.
    
    ### Events Recorded
    
    ☽'shadow Covens' Order forces engaged E'frostling positions at Terrace Momiou, citing recovery of a relic — designation unrecorded in this register; cross-reference ☽'somunis' Mist~Record, sealed — as justification under Foedus∴vincu. The action was not filed as conflict. The Order's initial report classified it as "reclamation of contested fire-core assets."
    
    The ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral was deployed against E'frostling tunnel-systems. Crystalline spirals froze entire corridors mid-collapse; flooding claimed the lower retreat chambers. Seventeen E'frostling guild-members; struck from register; fire-core allocation redistributed. Allied factions were drawn to the Terrace perimeter. Holdborn (ice-thresh) arrived after the lower galleries were already silent, finding char, brine, and fire-core fragments fused into the walls. The ice at Terrace Momiou now carries impressions. This is noted as material fact. Filed under; sealed; not read.
    
    ☽'ofund' Guild trade manifests from this period record crystal shipments through Terrace Momiou exceeding documented Aurora Stack exports by a factor of three. The discrepancy is attributed to ☽'aeteraea (Guild Member, Registry ☽-IV-0.22), whose coded ledger entries remain on file but undecoded by this office. Her records reference unnamed parties, unsanctioned routes. The manifests were filed. They were not challenged.
    
    One Iing zhixai'Ward, Aurora Stack (status: outlawed), appears in Guild route-interference logs — her discovery of Thaw-era passages disrupted tunnel-routes under ☽'ofund' charter. Economic impact: seventeen percent transit reduction along the ☽'Mavcaius corridor. That her own colony struck her from record is noted here without comment, with professional recognition.
    
    Reports of the plague-curse Mandatum∴absconditu surface in ☽'shadow Covens' Order medical filings, cross-referenced to weapons archives (Entry ☽-V-3.14, restricted). Accounts conflict regarding origin: relic exposure or crystalline feedback. The medical notations thin, become irregular, cease.
    
    Separately: ☽'ofund' Guild conducted supply interdiction against The Midnight Claws under Pactum∴ne emergency provisions. Records are incomplete. No formal denial-of-trade was registered with Parliament.
    
    ### Significance
    
    The Vum∴tenebra marks the first confirmed internal deployment of ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral against a Nightshelf-aligned population. Crystal stockpiles destroyed at the Terrace rendered the Flipper Accord inoperable; seven subsequent renegotiations have produced casualties at each round. The Foedus∴vincu provisions invoked by the Order were never formally challenged — no witness agreed to testify under Lex∴andatum protections. The law survived the conflagration. Its authority did not.
    
    ### Notable Figures
    
    — ☽'aeteraea, Guild Member, ☽'ofund' Guild. Trade-manifest discrepancies on file; coded entries unresolved.
    — Iing zhixai'Ward, formerly Aurora Stack, outlawed. Referenced in tunnel-route documentation only.
    — Niaecum~, ☽'ofund' Guild, veteran trader. Filed presence reports from Hearth Plaza, third-tier gallery, post-withdrawal.
    — Factor Umbrae ☽'Viaisnaum, Senior Archivist, ☽'ofund' Guild Registry. Author of this entry.
    
    ### Chronicler's Notes
    
    Watchers were reported in the tunnels around Terrace Momiou in the weeks following. This archivist does not speculate on their nature. The memorial stones at the Terrace's frozen edge bear names this office recognizes. They are the stones no one visits. What the fire remembers when the fire goes out is not within scope of this registry.
    
    It is on file.
    
    — ☽'Viaisnaum
