  annotation "note_1771579842313_0", anchor: "seven subsequent renegotiations have produced casualties at each round", text: "Seven *subsequent*. The administrative ice beneath Aurora Stack preserves three secret drafts of the Flipper Accord predating the public version — I extracted them myself from a stratum the Council prefers to consider empty. ☽'Viaisnaum treats the original Accord as a stable instrument the Vum∴tenebra shattered. It was already a fourth draft of a document no party fully accepted. Seven subsequent renegotiations brings us to eleven iterations at minimum. The Accord did not collapse at Terrace Momiou. It had never finished being built.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579842313_1", anchor: "Watchers were reported in the tunnels around Terrace Momiou in the weeks following", text: "☽'Viaisnaum's restraint — 'does not speculate' — is a filing convention I recognize because I use it. The Foundation Depths contain impressions from before penguin civilization: attentions, orientations, patient presences sealed in ice older than anything we have names for. When the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral froze those corridors mid-collapse, it cracked strata that had been closed since before settlement. What was reported afterward were not the newly dead. They were older than that. ☽'Viaisnaum sealed the file. I would have done the same. But 'does not speculate' and 'does not know' are different sentences.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579842313_2", anchor: "reclamation of contested fire-core assets", text: "\"Reclamation\" requires a prior claim. No Order filing in the Terrace Momiou administrative strata establishes one. The word does legal work it has not earned.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
